From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wevtapi: the Windows Event Log API over the event logs

wevtapi was a set of stubs: EvtQuery, EvtSubscribe, EvtOpenLog and the
enumerations returned nothing, EvtNext failed, and EvtRender,
EvtFormatMessage, EvtSeek, the publisher metadata calls and the rest were
not even exported. Get-WinEvent, .NET's EventLogReader/EventLogWatcher,
wevtutil-style tools and programs watching their own events found no
events.

The channels are the Event Log service's logs (advapi32: the logs under
...\Services\EventLog) and the channels described under WINEVT\Channels;
an event is one of their records, seen as the event schema has it
(Provider, EventID with Qualifiers, Level from the event type, Task from
the category, classic or audit Keywords, TimeCreated, EventRecordID,
Channel, Computer, Security UserID, EventData with Data and Binary).

- EvtQuery: an XPath filter (element and attribute steps, predicates,
  and/or/not(), comparisons, timediff(), band()) over a channel or an
  exported file, or a <QueryList> of Select and Suppress paths; forwards
  or backwards; several logs in time order; bad queries are
  ERROR_EVT_INVALID_QUERY, unknown channels ERROR_EVT_CHANNEL_NOT_FOUND
  (or a status, with EvtQueryTolerateQueryErrors). EvtNext, EvtSeek
  (first, last, current, bookmark; strict), EvtGetQueryInfo.
- EvtRender: the event's XML, a bookmark's XML, and values -- the system
  properties, the user data, or XPath values (typed as the system
  properties are). EvtCreateRenderContext checks its paths.
- EvtFormatMessage: the event's message from its source's message files
  (insertion strings, %%n parameters), its level, task (category),
  opcode, keyword, channel and provider names, a message by ID, and the
  XML with RenderingInfo.
- EvtSubscribe: pull (the signal event and EvtNext) and push
  (callbacks), to future events, from the oldest record or after a
  bookmark; new records are noticed through NotifyChangeEventLog.
- Bookmarks: EvtCreateBookmark (from XML), EvtUpdateBookmark.
- EvtOpenChannelEnum/EvtNextChannelPath, EvtOpenChannelConfig and its
  properties (from the logs' registry values: retention, auto backup,
  size, file, access; publishing values; the publisher list), set and
  saved with EvtSaveChannelConfig.
- EvtOpenLog/EvtGetLogInfo (times, size, attributes, records, oldest,
  full), EvtClearLog, EvtExportLog (a file the Event Log service reads
  back), EvtArchiveExportedLog.
- Publishers: the logs' sources and the publishers under
  WINEVT\Publishers; their metadata (GUID, message, parameter and
  resource files, channel references, levels, tasks from the categories,
  opcodes, keywords as object arrays); event metadata enumerations are
  empty (classic sources have no manifests).
- EvtOpenSession (this computer), EvtCancel, EvtClose, EvtGetEventInfo,
  EvtGetExtendedStatus. winevt.h gains the API's declarations.

Wine's wevtapi tests: 10 tests, no failures, as before.

Gate: test/evtquery-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/evtquery-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_QUERY_NOTHING, SG_MUTANT_NO_SUBSCRIPTION,
SG_MUTANT_NO_MESSAGE (wevtapi/main.c).
